# First ten minutes: the three beginner moves in one
# file — plot, solve, evaluate. Each is admitted without hidden defaults:
# the function call is spelled `sin(x)` (bare `sin` refuses, see
# tests/invalid/first_ten_minutes.emath), the solve world is declared
# (`over Real`) with the other candidates labeled by intent-completion, and
# the example binding feeds evaluation without a silent input default.
#
#   emath check tests/fixtures/language/intro/first-ten-minutes.emath
#   emath expand tests/fixtures/language/intro/first-ten-minutes.emath
#   emath exactness tests/fixtures/language/intro/first-ten-minutes.emath
plot sin(x)
solve x^2 = 2 over Real
y = x^2
example x = 2
